T2  - Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems
VL  - 37
ER  - 

TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Calibrated Trust in Language-Model Assistants Under Distribution Shift
AB  - People rely on language-model assistants more when the assistant sounds confident, whether or not it is right. We study how that reliance changes under distribution shift, where the assistant's accuracy drops but its stated confidence does not. In three preregistered experiments (N = 1,204) we find that verbalised uncertainty reduces over-reliance by 23% without reducing appropriate reliance, and that the effect survives a shift in task domain.
